I just remembered what you said about wanting to avoid the `CircuitInboundActivityContext` allocation when no one overrides `CreateInboundActivityHandler` in API review. To do that, you can compare the final and inner `Func<CircuitInboundActivityContext, Task>`.


```csharp
    private static Func<Func<Task>, Task> BuildInboundActivityDispatcher(IReadOnlyList<CircuitHandler> circuitHandlers, Circuit circuit)
    {
        var inner = static (CircuitInboundActivityContext context) => context.Handler();
        var next = inner;

        for (var i = circuitHandlers.Count - 1; i >= 0; i--)
        {
            next = circuitHandlers[i].CreateInboundActivityHandler(next);
        }

        if (next == inner)
        {
            // If no handlers wrapped inner, there is no need to allocate a context on each call.
            return static handler => handler();
        }

        return handler => next(new(handler, circuit));
    }
```
